---
# Checks that look for defects, not for a house style — layout is .clang-format's
# job, and the readability/modernize families disagree with this codebase on
# purpose (the one-line guards, `if (run.empty()) return;`, are deliberate).
#
# Pinned tool version: clang-tidy 22.1.8 (see .github/workflows/ci.yml).
Checks: >
  bugprone-*,
  cert-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  performance-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-exception-escape,
  -cert-err33-c,
  -performance-enum-size

# Every exclusion above, and why:
#
#   bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters
#     Fires on any two adjacent parameters of the same type — Cursor from, Cursor
#     to — which is most of the geometry in this program. It reports a shape, not
#     a mistake.
#   bugprone-exception-escape
#     main() can throw, because reading a file allocates. Silencing it properly
#     means wrapping main in a try/catch that prints something; worth doing one
#     day, not worth a lint gate blocking on it today.
#   cert-err33-c
#     Wants the return value of every printf, fputs and fwrite checked. In a
#     program whose whole output is a redrawn frame, there is nothing useful to do
#     with the count of bytes written.
#   performance-enum-size
#     Wants uint8_t bases on small enums. Real, and irrelevant at this scale.

WarningsAsErrors: '*'
HeaderFilterRegex: '.*'
